  "scope": "Task `f1347e0836ec`; selected generator version `2.1.0`; final SHA-256 `d11cf3efba53440d23c37196386a1ccfdb66e2fa3c3d20696bf7632c6632e76d`.\nDefect: coercive public call handling accepted bool/float/string seeds and sample indices plus negative sample indices; before battery was 11/12 with 33 strict-scalar findings.\nRepair: require exact integer `seed`/`sample_index` and reject negative `sample_index`; lawful integer generation, schedule, version, and approved distribution are unchanged.\nRacket authority: unchanged; `RULE_HASH=39c262fb60b4`; authority-set SHA-256 `89165aefa3732bcc7c01042b760757ed7b1038c18414f93aae2f73c9223ea3af`.\nChecks: strict after battery 12/12 green; portable selected-task tests 37/37; focused new tests 29/29 both in-place and after fresh patch replay.\nLessons: production sampler uses four ordered demonstrations plus one query; 300/300 lessons and 1,500/1,500 held-out query rotations had zero declared-rival ambiguity.\nSchedule: all four cyclic starts, 400 lessons per band and 1,200 total, had zero survivors among six live declared rivals after four demonstrations.\nPrototype: isolated proposed `trigger_diagonal \u2208 {main, anti}` extension covers both settings, exact canonical-default parity, distinct Racket programs, unique three-demo episodes, and public redaction.\nRemaining blocker: none for the selected repair; finite rival coverage, grid sizes 5..16, and prototype non-approval remain explicit limitations.\nAcceptance: routine.\n\n# Review details\n\n## Scope and provenance",
